// Signing configuration.
//
// The default below is AD-HOC: no team, no certificate, signed only for this
// machine. That is what a stranger cloning the repository gets, and it builds
// and runs. It does NOT survive distribution, and macOS re-prompts for
// Accessibility and Microphone after every rebuild, because both are bound to
// (bundle id + signature) and an ad-hoc signature changes with the binary.
// See "Build it yourself" in README.md.
//
// To sign with your own Apple Developer team, create App/Local.xcconfig —
// gitignored, never committed — from Local.xcconfig.example:
//
//     DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
//     CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic
//     CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development
//
// The optional include below is what picks it up. `#include?` does not fail
// when the file is absent, and xcconfig assignment is last-wins, so anything
// Local.xcconfig sets overrides the ad-hoc defaults above it.

DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -

#include? "Local.xcconfig"
